{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1355018-hobbyist-clique-and-object-fetishism-a-blood-sorcerer-s-wet-dream","id":1355018,"title":"Hobbyist Clique and Object Fetishism: A Blood Sorcerer's Wet Dream?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-15T09:23:46-08:00","id":1355018,"title":"Hobbyist Clique and Object Fetishism: A Blood Sorcerer's Wet Dream?","content":"[VTR 2e]<br /> <br /> As the post implies, is it possible to use Hobbyist Clique and Object Fetishism with Theban Sorcery &amp; Cruac?<br /> <br /> Hobbyist Clique mentions that whenever the support of the group is available, you get the 9-again quality on ANY rolls involving the group's chosen skill (Academics or Occult) and even goes on to say that you gain a +2 die bonus on extended actions. Due to the specific wording of &quot;any roll involving the group's skill&quot; I'd say that it should count, but I'm not sure. What is the general consensus?<br /> <br /> Object Fetishism: It specifically mentions how your character believes that the object has mystical or spiritual properties. You need to tie the object to a specific specialty (Theban or Cruac) and you gain extra Willpower each chapter equal to the merit's dots. If you spend that willpower you gain exceptional success on 3 instead of 5 successes whenever you're USING the specialty on a roll. Again, the wording is very general. If I can have specialty (Theban) and it helps me when casting rituals, then shouldn't object fetishism aid me as well? The Drawbacks are pretty heavy imo as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, what is the general consensus on using these two merits on Theban &amp; Cruac rolls? For me, object fetishism is easier to excuse but then again, if I were to put Majesty as a Specialty on my empathy rolls, does it work? That's what it gets down to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","user":"Hogsy","date":". 12-15-2019, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:07:16-08:00","id":1355051,"title":"","content":"My interpretation. <br /> Hobbyist Clique, you (the player) chooses one skill affiliated with your group and you get 9 again pertaining to that chosen skill. You do not get 9 again on every key skill affiliated with that group. <br /> <br /> I don't allow discipline specializations to apply to discipline or devotion activation rolls. You have to narrow it down to a specific power rank or devotion. <br /> <br /> As for the fetish, I would allow it to work with certain rituals or categories of ritual types but not all rituals. But yes, you could tie it to a sorcery specialty. And yes, this merit is a better benefit to Theban sorcerers than Acolytes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:06:07-08:00","id":1355063,"title":"","content":"Hobbyist Clique:<br /> <br /> Yes, but with major caveats. Remember that it's a social Merit, not just a boost to your rolls. Using this with a group of mortals is a major risk to the masquerade and your Humanity, because you have to tell them what you're working on to get their help. If you're working with supernaturals that aren't members of your Covenant... well... that's going to be a big problem there too. If you're just working within the Covenant &quot;hobbyist&quot; starts to be a stretch, and you have things like Altar and Lorekeeper which are generally a better investment.<br /> <br /> Object Fetishism:<br /> <br /> Maybe. First and foremost, you have to address that the drawback is designed for Integrity, and thus doesn't have a default Humanity level attached to it to say what the base dice-pool for the check would be. How you resolve this is going to majorly effect the impact of the Drawback, and if it should be allowed.<br /> <br /> After that, I agree that you shouldn't take Skill Specialties in a Discipline like that. While their are Specialties I would allow to apply to Theban or Cruac rituals, it wouldn't be an &quot;all of them&quot; sort of thing (like, say, &quot;Curses&quot; as an option).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:25:38-08:00","id":1355068,"title":"","content":"Hobbyist Clique does not explicitly apply to Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery rolls and therefore cannot be used for them, per the paragraph in &quot;The Request&quot; on page 151 of 2e Core.<br /> <br /> While I wouldn't make the call myself, Cr\u00faac and Theban Sorcery are specifically listed as example Specialties for Occult and Academics, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T15:26:38-08:00","id":1355070,"title":"","content":"The about using Hobbyist Clique, is that they'd need to be either blood sorcerers themselves or actually be there when the ritual is performed in order to apply the bonus to such a nice and specialized application of the skill. This isn't just sharing a knitting pattern or comparing methods of car maintenance, this is vampirc religious ceremonial sorcery. Not the kind of thing you'd find in a Facebook group, even one limited to skilled professionals.<br /> <br /> Edit: And I've been ninja'd with the actual rules. I've got to go through and reread my library at some point if I'm going to post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T16:02:17-08:00","id":1355078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1355018-hobbyist-clique-and-object-fetishism-a-blood-sorcerer-s-wet-dream?p=1355068#post1355068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hobbyist Clique does not explicitly apply to Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery rolls and therefore cannot be used for them, per the paragraph in &quot;The Request&quot; on page 151 of 2e Core.<br /> <br /> While I wouldn't make the call myself, Cr\u00faac and Theban Sorcery are specifically listed as example Specialties for Occult and Academics, respectively.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That specifies extended actions though, not the 9-again quality or object fetishism (for example, Patient doesn't benefit Theban).<br /> <br /> If Academics &amp; Occult didn't specify Theban &amp; Cruac as specialties, I wouldn't even think about this, but they do.. In addition to that, Hobbyist Clique mentions that it benefits any roll involving said skill. I understand the risks but what I had in mind was to use five 1-dot Ghouls as my hobbyist clique basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T16:13:32-08:00","id":1355080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hogsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1355018-hobbyist-clique-and-object-fetishism-a-blood-sorcerer-s-wet-dream?p=1355078#post1355078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That specifies extended actions though, not the 9-again quality or object fetishism (for example, Patient doesn't benefit Theban).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hobbyist Clique is a Merit that modifies extended actions and the only way to use it on Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery is by benefiting their extended actions, because extended actions are how blood sorcery works mechanically. The Merit does not explicitly apply to Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery and therefore cannot be used for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:04:48-08:00","id":1355086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1355018-hobbyist-clique-and-object-fetishism-a-blood-sorcerer-s-wet-dream?p=1355080#post1355080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hobbyist Clique is a Merit that modifies extended actions and the only way to use it on Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery is by benefiting their extended actions, because extended actions are how blood sorcery works mechanically. The Merit does not explicitly apply to Cr\u00faac or Theban Sorcery and therefore cannot be used for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But the 9-again bonus is applied to any roll using the chosen Skill, not specifically extended actions so it doesn't need to specify that it works with Sorceries. It merely states that when rolling extended actions, you gain an additional +2 die bonus on them, which doesn't apply to Sorceries because it doesn't specify it. I do see your point however and it does make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T17:38:44-08:00","id":1355091,"title":"","content":"Trying to rules-lawyer it is an argument to take to your group. With that reference? It seems pretty clear that VtR2e wants to make is so general Merits don't apply to blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> All in all, it seems a bit pointless. It's not like there aren't options in the book to get better rolls.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T18:05:57-08:00","id":1355096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1355018-hobbyist-clique-and-object-fetishism-a-blood-sorcerer-s-wet-dream?p=1355091#post1355091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to rules-lawyer it is an argument to take to your group. With that reference? It seems pretty clear that VtR2e wants to make is so general Merits don't apply to blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> All in all, it seems a bit pointless. It's not like there aren't options in the book to get better rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, Temple of Damnation isn't an option so there's only Library left to boost my rolls which is why I was looking for additional ways to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25190-hogsy","name":"Hogsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T04:21:58-08:00","id":1355159,"title":"","content":"You can meditate for up to +3, you have Library for up to +3, Flock for regaining WP that Theban uses up, Stigmata that gives you 8-again on Theban rolls if you ingest that blood that scene, and the Lorekeeper Merit which lets you get Herd and Retainer for free that you could append Flock and Stigmata to.<br /> <br /> What more do you need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}